## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | **1 (systemic — affects 8 of 10 tests)** |
| **High** | 1 |
| **Medium** | 2 |
| **Low** | 1 |

This suite is the poster child for "95% coverage, 0% confidence." Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called, but **8 of 10 tests either have no assertion at all or only assert `IsNotNull`** — a check so weak it can never fail for value types and almost never fails for the collection-returning methods here. You are exercising lines without verifying behavior.

---

### Critical

#### 1. **Coverage-Touching / No-Assertion Tests** — systemic across entire file

The suite methodically calls every public method on `ProductCatalog` without verifying outcomes. This is the single root cause of production bugs slipping through.

| Test (line) | What it does | What it proves |
|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` (L17) | Calls `AddProduct` | Nothing — no assertion |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` (L31) | Calls `UpdatePrice` | Nothing — no assertion |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` (L39) | Calls `RemoveProduct` | Nothing — no assertion |
| `GetProductCount_Works` (L63) | Calls `GetProductCount` | Nothing — no assertion, result discarded |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L69) | Calls `ApplyBulkDiscount` | Nothing — no assertion |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85) | Calls `ImportFromCsv` | Nothing — no assertion |
| `GetProduct_Works` (L23) | Asserts `IsNotNull` on result | Only that something was returned — not that it's the *right* product |
| `SearchProducts_Works` (L46) | Asserts `IsNotNull` on results | Only that a list was returned — not its contents or count |
| `GetAllProducts_Works` (L55) | Asserts `IsNotNull` on `all` | Same — never checks the list has any items |
| `ExportToCsv_Works` (L77) | Asserts `IsNotNull` on csv | Never checks the CSV content |

**Concrete fixes (before → after):**

```csharp
// AddProduct_Works → verify the product is actually persisted
var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
```

```csharp
// UpdatePrice_Works → verify the price actually changed
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
```

